subproblems.statement:
Let n, ℓ ∈ ℕ, let W ⊆ ℝ^{n+ℓ} = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin (n+ℓ)) be a linear subspace with dim W = n, and let P := W.starProjection : ℝ^{n+ℓ} → ℝ^{n+ℓ} be the orthogonal projection onto W. Then there is a map f : ℝ^{n+ℓ} → ℝⁿ = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) such that:
(i) f is 1-Lipschitz;
(ii) for all a, b ∈ ℝ^{n+ℓ}, f(a) = f(b) ⟺ P(a) = P(b);
(iii) for every set S ⊆ ℝ^{n+ℓ} (arbitrary), Hⁿ(P(S)) = Lⁿ(f(S)).
Here Hⁿ := μHE[n] (outer measure) on ℝ^{n+ℓ}, and Lⁿ := volume (Lebesgue outer measure) on ℝⁿ.
